WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:12.799
In January 2021, a mob occupied the US Capitol, seeking
to overturn the results of the presidential election.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:15.839
This was a call to duty for America's educators.

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:19.680
While the Capitol attack was
precipitated by former president Trump's

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.439
caustic lies, the poisonous polarization it reflected

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:27.527
can be traced to weakness in the nation's civic foundation.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:31.554
Just a fraction of Americans can name
the three branches of government

00:00:31.554 --> 00:00:34.079
or pass the nation's citizenship test.

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:39.632
Most republicans thought Trump's 2016 
presidential election victory was fair,

00:00:39.632 --> 00:00:41.918
but that his 2020 defeat wasn't.

00:00:41.918 --> 00:00:46.960
More than 90 percent of democrats
said Joe Biden's 2020 election was fair,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.456
but nearly half said
Hillary Clinton's 2016 defeat wasn't.

00:00:51.456 --> 00:00:57.584
Democracy doesn't work if voters only trust 
elections when their side carries the day.

00:00:57.584 --> 00:01:02.320
This is a test of our civic mettle.
Our schools and colleges have a crucial

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.880
role to play in helping us pass that test.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.867
Do you think it's a problem that most
Americans can't pass the nation's citizenship test?

00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:14.240
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.439
what other topics you'd like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:22.415
and be sure to like and subscribe for
more research and videos from AEI.

